---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import ArticleSchema from '../../components/ArticleSchema.astro';
import TldrBox from '../../components/TldrBox.astro';
import FaqSection from '../../components/FaqSection.astro';
import { site, description, pageTitle } from '../../content';
import { appBySlug } from '../../data/apps';

const a = appBySlug('activecampaign')!;
const b = appBySlug('recart')!;
const path = '/compare/activecampaign-vs-recart';
const title = pageTitle(site, 'compare/activecampaign-vs-recart');
const desc = description(site, 'compare/activecampaign-vs-recart');
const faqs = [
  {
    "question": "When should I compare ActiveCampaign with Recart?",
    "answer": "Compare ActiveCampaign when your team will own follow-up automation. Evaluate Recart for sms ownership beside email; demonstrate the required event and operating handoff before choosing."
  },
  {
    "question": "Do these pages establish a recovery winner?",
    "answer": "No merchant trial or incremental lift is established. The workflows and numeric examples are proposed evaluation tools."
  },
  {
    "question": "How should I plan timing and incentives?",
    "answer": "Choose timing from checkout behavior and operating constraints. Recheck purchase, inventory, permission and competing queues at dispatch; no universal timing or discount cap is established."
  },
  {
    "question": "What does the numeric example assume?",
    "answer": "A $409 basket at 68% gross margin has $278.12 gross profit at full price. A 8% code removes $32.72 from revenue with unchanged goods cost, before other variable costs."
  }
];
---
<BaseLayout title={title} description={desc} site={site} path={path}>
<ArticleSchema title={title} description={desc} siteName={site.name} domain={site.domain} path={path} />
<section class="py-16"><div class="container">
<a href="/compare" class="link">← Comparisons</a>
<h1 class="hero-title mt-6">{a.name} vs {b.name} for Shopify cart recovery</h1>
<p class="mt-7 text-xl">SMS ownership beside email: compare event coverage, operator responsibilities and recovery cost with your own Shopify checkout.</p>
<TldrBox picks={[{label:"ActiveCampaign",tool:a.name,reason:"An internal owner maintains email recovery and follow-up branches."},{label:"Recart",tool:b.name,reason:"SMS marketing and list growth, with managed service options."}]} />
<article class="prose-shopify mt-12 max-w-4xl">
<table class="data-table"><thead><tr><th>Decision</th><th>ActiveCampaign</th><th>Recart</th></tr></thead><tbody>
<tr><td>Evaluation focus</td><td>Cart-triggered email and your team’s follow-up rules</td><td>SMS marketing and list growth, with managed service options.</td></tr>
<tr><td>Demonstration</td><td>Checkout event, populated cart block and purchase exit</td><td>SMS ownership beside email and purchase suppression</td></tr>
<tr><td>Budget</td><td>Current quote for audience, automation and implementation</td><td>Current quote including required channels and service scope</td></tr>
</tbody></table>
<h2>Decide whether SMS fills a real gap</h2>
<p>Recart currently presents itself as SMS marketing and list growth, with email-provider integrations. Compare it as an SMS owner alongside your email workflow, rather than assuming it replaces ActiveCampaign email or provides push reminders. Its managed-service page describes onboarding and campaign work, with service inclusion tied to plan; confirm your exact scope.</p>
<h2>Follow the signup offer into recovery</h2>
<p>A mobile shopper may join through a popup, receive a welcome offer and abandon a basket minutes later. Propose that journey with a test profile. Record which system stores email permission, which stores SMS permission and which owns the offer. Check coupon combinations in Shopify before enabling a second recovery discount. An email signup must not silently become an SMS subscription.</p>
<h2>Make the two queues visible</h2>
<p>Assign ActiveCampaign email and Recart SMS a shared customer and order identifier in your operating record. Demonstrate the actual integration or handoff before relying on it. Purchase between the email and scheduled text, unsubscribe before the text, and repeat the checkout event. Inspect each queue for cancellation and duplicate entry. If one system cannot see the necessary state, keep that branch paused until an owner can reconcile it.</p>
<h2>Give the managed SMS team a release contract</h2>
<p>Specify who approves creative, holiday changes, audience exclusions and emergency pauses. For an international shipping objection, answer the shipping question before proposing urgency. For an unavailable size, avoid returning the shopper to an impossible basket. Compare operator effort and per-destination messaging costs with keeping recovery email alone. Vendor revenue claims and click attribution do not establish incremental lift for this pair.</p>
<h2>Check the ActiveCampaign event before designing branches</h2>
<p><a href="https://help.activecampaign.com/hc/en-us/articles/360001045964-Abandoned-cart-overview">ActiveCampaign’s cart documentation</a> describes email automation and a cart content block. For Shopify it documents a checkout-stage requirement for data sync. A product-page visitor or anonymous cart is not automatically eligible. Record the integration wait and workflow delay separately, then inspect the actual event payload and destination.</p>
<h2>Retain margin math without implying results</h2>
<p>Illustrative basket: $409 at 68% gross margin has $130.88 goods cost and $278.12 full-price gross profit. A 8% code leaves $376.28 revenue and $245.40 gross profit, a $32.72 reduction. Goods cost is unchanged. Subtract fulfillment, payment, message and return costs before calling the remainder contribution. This does not show an incremental recovery by either product.</p>
<h2>Cut over and measure deliberately</h2>
<p>Inventory Shopify and provider recovery flows, pause competing queues and assign one owner per event and channel. Reconcile opt-outs and purchases before enabling the replacement. Compare deduplicated contribution per eligible shopper over the same window. If a randomized no-message group is feasible, choose allocation and duration from traffic, conversion delay and the effect you need to detect. Keep a rollback owner for broken links or failed purchase exits.</p>
<p>Product scope checked November 25, 2026: <a href="https://recart.com/fully-managed-sms">Recart primary documentation</a>. Select the setup whose demonstrated workflow and staffing model fit your store; no ratings or universal winner are supplied.</p>
</article>
<FaqSection faqs={faqs} title={`${a.name} vs ${b.name} FAQ`} />
</div></section></BaseLayout>
